  "body": "From https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1659218.\r\n\r\nCurrently [the spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#the-input-element:legacy-canceled-activation-behavior) says it runs when the element's type attribute \"is\" checkbox or radio. It introduces an unexpected behavior when a click event listener changes the type: the input element remains \"checked\" even when it's not a checkbox or a radio.\r\n\r\nTry it here and see \"radio1.checked === true\" on Chrome: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/attachment.cgi?id=9172764\r\n\r\nGecko runs it based on the previous state, and I think the spec should also follow the Gecko behavior.\r\n\r\ncc @smaug---- ",
